3. Treat any job exit 137 as a memory bug to fix. Never retry it as-is. Report it in your next STATE.
4. Clean up: run `bin/job kill gold-rerun-b5` and `bin/job kill e4b-timing-wait3`. Journal both.
5. e4b-timing (critical path, still first priority): the waiter died, but the Kaggle kernel runs remotely. Before you push anything, check `kaggle kernels status aniket0202/gemma-e4b-timing` and pull its output. If v3 completed, use its output: do the dec-018 4-L4 guard check first, then timing_summary. If it's still running, relaunch only the waiter with bin/job. Push a new version only if v3 actually failed, and log it in ops/budget/kaggle.md. Don't spend quota twice on the same run.
